{"step_index":1069,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:19:55Z","thinking":"**Investigating HTTPS Proxy Configuration**\n\nPort 80 is unavailable, strongly suggesting the service operates on HTTPS over port 9443. The backup configuration has lines related to proxying that were commented out. Those commented lines likely hold a clue, especially `proxy_set_header Host` and `X-Forwarded-Port`. Examining the active configuration file `03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf` is the next step.\n\n\n**Analyzing Proxy Header Overrides**\n\nThe configuration includes `include nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf`, which sets several proxy headers, including `Host`, `X-Forwarded-Host`, and `X-Forwarded-Port`. The `proxy_set_header Host $http_host;` directive likely overwrites the `Host` header, and this needs further investigation. Removing `include` and modifying header configurations will reveal how the headers are ultimately set. It's crucial to understand the combined effect of these directives.\n\n\n**Comparing Direct Access and Proxying**\n\nDirect access to the application endpoint at `172.30.198.50:9443` is returning a 200 status, while accessing via the proxy (`172.30.198.33:9443`) results in a 400. This suggests a difference in the requests or responses. The direct test likely bypasses the proxy configurations.\n\n**Identifying Missing Request Headers**\n\nTo pinpoint the discrepancy, a listener on port 9444 will capture requests sent to a test virtual host that proxies through the listener. The goal is to compare headers sent directly versus those forwarded by the proxy. Examining these headers should reveal missing information or incorrectly configured forwarding.\n\n**Implementing a Request Interception**\n\nA temporary virtual host will be established locally to listen on an unused port (9440) and forward requests to the listener on port 9444, capturing headers. This setup allows for detailed inspection of what nginx is sending upstream to Tomcat to diagnose the issue.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/home/koby/.ansible/kssh th2-revproxyp-fe1 'python3 -c \"\nimport socket, threading, time, urllib.request\n\ndef srv():\n    s = socket.socket()\n    s.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_REUSEADDR, 1)\n    s.bind((\\\"127.0.0.1\\\", 9444))\n    s.listen(1)\n    c, _ = s.accept()\n    raw = c.recv(4096)\n    print(\\\"=== CAPTURED FROM NGINX ===\\\")\n    print(raw.decode(\\\"latin1\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\"))\n    c.sendall(b\\\"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\\r\\nContent-Length: 2\\r\\n\\r\\nOK\\\")\n    c.close()\n    s.close()\n\nt = threading.Thread(target=srv)\nt.start()\ntime.sleep(0.5)\n\n# Write temp nginx config\nimport subprocess\ncfg = \\\"\\\"\\\"server {\n    listen 127.0.0.1:9440;\n    location / {\n        include nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf;\n        proxy_set_header Host \\$http_host;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Ssl on;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;\n        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:9444;\n    }\n}\\\"\\\"\\\"\nsubprocess.run([\\\"sudo\\\", \\\"tee\\\", \\\"/etc/nginx/conf.d/test_proxy.conf\\\"], input=cfg.encode())\nsubprocess.run([\\\"sudo\\\", \\\"nginx\\\", \\\"-s\\\", \\\"reload\\\"])\ntime.sleep(0.5)\n\n# Send request through test proxy\ntry:\n    req = urllib.request.Request(\\\"http://127.0.0.1:9440/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health\\\", headers={\\\"Host\\\": \\\"map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443\\\"})\n    urllib.request.urlopen(req)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\\\"Err:\\\", e)\n\nt.join(timeout=3)\nsubprocess.run([\\\"sudo\\\", \\\"rm\\\", \\\"-f\\\", \\\"/etc/nginx/conf.d/test_proxy.conf\\\"])\nsubprocess.run([\\\"sudo\\\", \\\"nginx\\\", \\\"-s\\\", \\\"reload\\\"])\n\"'","Cwd":"/home/koby","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Capturing exact proxy request","toolSummary":"Capture Nginx proxy headers"}}]}
